(Bug #86 - a float's precision was dropped by every sink but Print.
 `{ratio:.2}` printed 2.50 to the terminal and 2.5 into a text
 initializer, a buffer set/copy/append, a `write` and a function
 argument: the precision reached one printer that only Print called,
 and every other sink appended the float through a routine that takes
 the raw bits alone and has nowhere to put N. A receipt written to a
 file therefore disagreed with the same line shown on screen.

 LANGUAGE.md "Format Strings Everywhere" promises format specifiers
 "render identically whether the result is printed, written to a file,
 or built into a text or a buffer", so every line below must read the
 same. Fixed the way #44 fixed `{list}`: the one renderer is redirected
 at the destination buffer, never copied into a second buffer-shaped
 printer.)

To announce with a text called label.
  Print label.

a float called ratio is 2.5.

Print "print:    {ratio:.2}".

a text called said is "text:     {ratio:.2}".
Print said.

Create a buffer called copied.
copy "copy:     {ratio:.2}" to copied.
Print copied.

Create a buffer called kept.
set kept to "set:      {ratio:.2}".
Print kept.

Create a buffer called grown.
copy "append:   " to grown.
append "{ratio:.2}" to grown.
Print grown.

Open a file at 1 for writing called out.
write "write:    {ratio:.2}\n" to out.

announce with "argument: {ratio:.2}".

(The receipt case, all the way to disk and back: the bytes on the file
 are the bytes the terminal showed, not a rounder-looking neighbour.)
Open a file for writing called receipt at "./test_float_precision_sink.txt".
write "file:     {ratio:.2}\n" to receipt.
Close receipt.
Create a buffer called line.
Open a file for reading called back at "./test_float_precision_sink.txt".
Read line from back into line.
Close back.
(`Read line` keeps the trailing newline it found, as documented, so this
 print must not add a second one.)
Print line without newline.
Delete the file "./test_float_precision_sink.txt".
